        "title": "Topology - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The central question: **when are two spaces \"the same\"?**\nTopology makes \"same\" mean \"homeomorphic\" (continuous bijection with continuous inverse).\nTwo spaces are topologically equivalent if one can be continuously deformed into the other\nwithout tearing or gluing."
    },
