        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Topology - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A metric d(x,y) gives concrete distances.\nA topology specifies which sets are \"open\" — the abstract structure."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#008",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:topology:00-overview, git-history:topology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "topology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "topology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:topology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "topology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Topology - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "WHY GENERALIZE FROM METRIC?\n  Products of infinitely many metric spaces need not be metrizable.\n  Weak topology on Banach space (functional analysis) is not metric.\n  Algebraic geometry's Zariski topology is not even Hausdorff!\n  The \"correct\" notion of continuity is open-set preservation."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#009",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:topology:00-overview, git-history:topology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "topology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "topology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:topology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "topology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Topology - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "OPEN SET AXIOMS:\n  1. ∅ and X are open.\n  2. Arbitrary unions of open sets are open.\n  3. Finite intersections of open sets are open."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#010",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:topology:00-overview, git-history:topology:00-overview]",
