      "text": "## Why Topology Matters"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#013",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:topology:00-overview, git-history:topology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "topology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "topology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:topology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "topology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Topology - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nANALYSIS CONNECTION:\n  Completeness, convergence, compactness — all topological.\n  Uniform continuity needs metric; continuity needs only topology.\n  The Baire Category Theorem (complete metric spaces) ← used everywhere in analysis.\n  Banach's fixed point theorem ← contractive maps on complete metric spaces."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#014",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:topology:00-overview, git-history:topology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "topology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "topology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:topology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "topology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Topology - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "ALGEBRA CONNECTION:\n  The Galois group Gal(Q̄/Q) carries a profinite topology.\n  Algebraic K-theory uses topology of classifying spaces BGL(R).\n  Lie groups: groups that are also smooth manifolds."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#015",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
